      "merge_method": "squash",
      "commit_title": "perf(file): avoid opening files for file_size (#7481)",
      "commit_message": "`file_size()` now retrieves the size of whole-file references directly\nfrom object metadata instead of loading each file through\n`DaftFile::load()`.\n\nThis avoids the unnecessary `supports_range()` probe and reader\nconstruction that previously happened after the file size had already\nbeen fetched. The function is now an async scalar UDF, allowing\nindependent size lookups in a batch to run concurrently.\n\nByte-range file references retain the existing load behavior so their\nreturned size semantics are unchanged.\n\nAdded coverage for multiple file inputs and null propagation.\n\nFixes #7480 \n\n- `cargo check -p daft-file`\n- `make build`\n- `DAFT_RUNNER=native make test EXTRA_ARGS='-v\ntests/file/test_file_basics.py -k filesize'`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: yang3.xie <yang3.xie@ly.com>"
    },
